sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Gate Admin
    participant Gate as eFTI Gate (eu-ee31)
    participant GateReg as GateRegistry (in-memory)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant OtherNode as Gate Node 2 (eu-ee31)

    Note over Gate,OtherNode: Multi-node deployment: both nodes share the same<br/>PostgreSQL. GateRegistry is an in-memory cache of<br/>the latest gates row per id (loaded at startup).

    Admin->>+Gate: POST /api/v1/gates<br/>Authorization: Bearer <TARA-JWT, role=ADMIN>
    Note over Admin,Gate: JSON body (camelCase per OpenAPI GateWrite):<br/>{"id":"eu-pl01","countryCode":"PL",<br/>"eDeliveryUrl":"https://efti.gitd.gov.pl/as4",<br/>"eDeliveryCert":"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----..."}

    Gate->>Gate: Validate JWT (signature, exp, iss, aud);<br/>require resource_access.efti-gate.roles ∋ ADMIN
    Gate->>+GateReg: save(Gate{id="eu-pl01", ...})

    GateReg->>GateReg: in-memory cache: gates["eu-pl01"] = Gate{...}<br/>(this node only)

    GateReg->>+DB: In a single transaction: append a new gates row for 'eu-pl01'<br/>and emit a registry_change_gates notification carrying the gate id.
    DB-->>-GateReg: written (new row; latest row for id wins on next read)

    Note over DB,OtherNode: The notification is emitted by the application inside<br/>the same transaction as the INSERT — there is no DB-side trigger.<br/>The notification is delivered to LISTENers on transaction commit.

    DB->>OtherNode: NOTIFY registry_change_gates (channel: registry_change_gates, payload: eu-pl01)

    OtherNode->>OtherNode: Listen thread receives notification
    OtherNode->>+DB: Resolve the latest gates row for id='eu-pl01'
    DB-->>-OtherNode: latest Gate{id="eu-pl01", …}
    OtherNode->>OtherNode: gateRegistry.gates["eu-pl01"] = Gate{...}
    Note over OtherNode: In-memory registry updated on Node 2<br/>without restart.

    GateReg->>GateReg: notifyChanged(gate) → internal listeners
    GateReg-->>-Gate: done

    Gate->>+Gate: runCatching { ping(gate.id) }
    Note over Gate: Auto-ping new gate after registration to verify connectivity.<br/>A successful ping appends another gates row carrying status='ONLINE'<br/>and last_ping_at=NOW().

    Gate-->>-Admin: 201 Created\n{"id":"eu-pl01","countryCode":"PL","status":"ONLINE","isActive":true,...}
